WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.449 --> 00:00:03.470
Welcome to day 10 of the TSA Dragster build,

1
00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:06.280
our sprint 2 dry fit assembly check.

2
00:00:06.809 --> 00:00:07.949
Walking into the shop today,

3
00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.529
your specific goal is to temporarily install both axles,

4
00:00:11.729 --> 00:00:15.090
all 4 plastic wheels and the 2 bottom eye screws.

5
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:16.450
Once assembled,

6
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:20.610
you need to verify that your eye screws are at least 150 millimeters apart

7
00:00:20.889 --> 00:00:23.209
and weigh your car on the digital scale to make

8
00:00:23.209 --> 00:00:25.670
sure it meets the 40 g minimum mass rule.

9
00:00:26.049 --> 00:00:27.290
During the first half of class,

10
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.799
you get all of your materials and the dry fit assembly goes smoothly.

11
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.360
You slide both axles through the body and attach the four plastic wheels.

12
00:00:35.889 --> 00:00:37.909
When you set the car on the flat test table,

13
00:00:38.169 --> 00:00:40.450
all four wheels touch the surface evenly and

14
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.590
roll straight without rubbing the wood body.

15
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:43.810
Next,

16
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.319
you flip the car over

17
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.759
and measure your two centerline eye screws with a metric ruler,

18
00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:52.400
confirming they sit at a legal 160 millimeters apart.

19
00:00:52.939 --> 00:00:54.459
With 5 minutes left in class,

20
00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.830
you place your complete dry fit car on the digital scale

21
00:00:57.979 --> 00:01:00.000
and hit a major bottleneck.

22
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.680
The scale reads 37.1 g.

23
00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:06.559
That puts your car 2.9 g under the 40 g minimum weight limit,

24
00:01:07.019 --> 00:01:09.900
which means automatic disqualification at race check-in.

25
00:01:10.519 --> 00:01:11.870
Looking at the TSA rules,

26
00:01:11.919 --> 00:01:13.790
you know add-on weights aren't allowed,

27
00:01:14.239 --> 00:01:18.860
but you are allowed up to 10 metal washers on the axles plus primer and paint.

28
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.300
Now it is your turn to document today's shop session before leaving class.

29
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.459
Scroll down to the activity form right below this video

30
00:01:26.599 --> 00:01:29.220
and write a complete 3-part daily work log.

31
00:01:29.639 --> 00:01:32.040
Be sure to state today's specific build goal,

32
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.110
record the exact work accomplished,

33
00:01:34.279 --> 00:01:34.790
measurements,

34
00:01:34.849 --> 00:01:37.800
and the 37.1 g weight bottleneck you discovered.

35
00:01:38.279 --> 00:01:40.720
Write your immediate steps for tomorrow's class so

36
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.629
your car reaches the 40 g minimum.

37
00:01:42.959 --> 00:01:46.459
Remember that your teacher has told you paint and washers can be used to add weight.

38
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.559
4 washers weigh 1 g and 1 coat of paint is about 1 g of weight.